From e1d301b4035cab538d6e406db48d53875b8e9215 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:43:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] mach-snapdragon: add HiBy RS6 off-mode charging

Plugging a charger into a powered-off RS6 makes the PMIC power it on.
Stock Android handles that with a charger mode; without it the board
would boot the OS. When the pm660 PON reason is USB charger only (and
there is no warm reset reason), stay in U-Boot: keep the panel dark,
show the battery level from the cw2015 for a few seconds on any button
press, boot on a long power-key press and power off when the charger is
removed.

Enabled with CONFIG_QCOM_HIBY_RS6_CHARGER (board/qualcomm/hiby-rs6.config)
and gated at runtime on the "hiby,rs6" compatible.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SXjPGasJxD6XRYU1J9jsnW
---
